Z||000000||jlruiz67||01-27-2001||04:05 PM||||Hello all<P> I have a Compaq 1750 with docking station in trade for a set of Exhaust Headers Installed. I was going to fix my stock manifolds but if some one is up to trade parts and labor for the laptop that I'm using right now I would go for it. I'm in Orange County, So California. Lets talk.||||reg||14
Z||000001||Seanh||01-27-2001||04:14 PM||||Interesting Trade! If I lived closer I would be tempted to take you up on it. Sounds like a pretty good trade. Perhaps FieroShop (I think he's in your area) needs a computer. You know, you can get some top quality headers for around $700. Should be all that hard to install for a Fiero Guy.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||jlruiz67||01-27-2001||04:23 PM||||Well the thing is that I was going to just replace the stock manifold with stock manifold but I tought that maybe I could trade my laptop for the headers I can't afford other wise. I hope some one in So California is interested||||reg||1
