Z||000004||jlruiz67||01-28-2001||01:09 PM||||Can anyone tell me the real risk of running my Fiero with a huge leak on my exhaust manifold for a couple of weeks, I don't want to mess anything else up but I do need to use a car to go to work and back and I'm short on cash for a rental, That is one of the reasons why I want to do the trade.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||01-28-2001||02:54 PM||||The only risk I know of it being to loud. I dont think there is any problem with running with an exhaust leak. I drove mine for over 7 months with craked manifolds. The only thing I could see being a problem is fumes in the engine compartment, but I never had any trouble.||||reg||1
Z||000006||jlruiz67||01-28-2001||04:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>The only risk I know of it being to loud. I dont think there is any problem with running with an exhaust leak. I drove mine for over 7 months with craked manifolds. The only thing I could see being a problem is fumes in the engine compartment, but I never had any trouble.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>How bad was yours? My manifold is almost completly from the Y pipe and its really loud. Is it possible to damage anything internaly? <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||01-28-2001||05:53 PM||||Not really. There will be a decrease in overall car engine performance, but no damage. By letting this problem go, then you will damage your exhaust manifolds more then they are now, but thats not a big deal if your planning on going with headers. Despite how hard it looks, they are really not all that bad to take off. Just make sure your bolts are all tightened up so you dont strip out your holes on the engine. The way you are describing (since I cant see it in person) sounds more like maybe a bad gasket or loose bolts. Cracks will allow some extra noise, but unless it is a huge crack, probally not as much as you are getting. Just doulble check the bolts to make sure they dont strip out your engine threads, thats all I am concerned with. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||jlruiz67||01-28-2001||06:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>sounds more like maybe a bad gasket or loose bolts. Cracks will allow some extra noise, but unless it is a huge crack, probally not as much as you are getting. Just doulble check the bolts to make sure they dont strip out your engine threads, thats all I am concerned with. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yes is a huge crack, I think it goes all the way arrownd the pipe, it almost like the first cylinder had no manifold its a nasty huge crack, I had noticed in the past some noice but I tought it was my mufler but after replacing that the noise didn't really go all away, I hope I do find some one I could trade with otherwize I will go with stock manifolds and put them in myself.<P>If anyone in So California want to trade a set of FOCOA OR Chris West headers istalled for a Compaq Armada 1750 please email me. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||2xsess||01-28-2001||07:50 PM||||The whole headers thing has been discussed here a few times, unless you're running some kind of highly modified engine a set of ported stock manifolds will deliver the same performance increase as the headers and at way less cost.<P>The lack of back pressure will cause loss of performance. If you let it go an exteneded amount of time it will eventually start to do some harm.<P>A guy named Lanny Voight had a set of ported manifolds he was trying to sell about 2 weeks ago. I think he wanted like $100 for them , try emailing him and seeing if he still has them. <BR>lannyv@worldnet.att.net<P>Good luck<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">    <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||danny boy||01-28-2001||10:06 PM|||| The guy I bought my GT off of had let an exaust leak go for a while...ended up melting the fuel pump relay and the other relay beside it wiring harness.||||reg||1
